INT. WAYNE MANOR - STUDY - DAWN

The first rays of sunrise peek through the grand windows. Andrea sits in a comfortable leather chair while Alfred serves tea. Bruce, now changed from his Batman attire, stands by the fireplace.

ALFRED
(pouring tea)
I must say, your handling of Dr. Price was most impressive. Though I suspected something was amiss when she declined to attend any of the staff luncheons.

ANDREA
(accepting tea gratefully)
Sometimes the smallest details tell the biggest stories.

BRUCE
(thoughtfully)
The robbery patterns, the chemical compounds, the Arkham connection - you pieced it together perfectly, Andrea. Gotham owes you a debt.

ALFRED
(with a knowing smile)
Perhaps, sir, this partnership might become a more permanent arrangement?

Andrea takes a moment to look around the study, noting the morning light casting shadows that seem less threatening than those in Arkham.

ANDREA
(with quiet confidence)
Gotham needs all the help it can get. And I have to admit, working with Batman has been... enlightening.

BRUCE
(extending hand)
Welcome to the team, Detective.

The morning sun fully breaks through the windows, marking the dawn of a new day for Gotham's protectors.

===GAME END===

