INT. SATRIALE'S BACK ROOM - LATE AFTERNOON

Silvio leads Vincent past hanging prosciuttos and shelves of canned tomatoes. The meat locker hums in the background.

SILVIO
(checking they're alone)
Tony's got a job for you. Consider it your chance to get back in rhythm.

He pulls out a folded piece of paper.

SILVIO
There's a card game tonight at the Executive Card Club. Commissioner Anderson's gonna be there. Tony wants you to observe only. Don't approach, don't interact. Just watch his playing style, who he talks to, how much he loses.

Vincent takes the paper containing the address.

SILVIO
(firmly)
This time, you wait for Tony to ask for the information. Capisce? And Vincent... you're going as a player, not a wise guy. Business casual, like those Wall Street types.

He checks his watch.

SILVIO
Game starts at nine. And remember - you're just another degenerate gambler tonight. Nothing more.
===GAME END===

