INT. BADA BING BACK ROOM - NIGHT - CONTINUING

Vincent stands slowly, maintaining his composure. He straightens his jacket, wincing slightly from the earlier confrontation. Without a word, he gives Tony a respectful nod.

The room remains tensely silent as Vincent walks toward the exit. Christopher moves to escort him, but Tony raises a hand.

TONY
(quietly to others)
Let him walk out on his own.

Vincent reaches the door, his hand on the handle. Behind him, the familiar sounds of the club begin to resume - ice in glasses, quiet murmurs of conversation.

SILVIO
(to Tony, just loud enough for Vincent to hear)
At least he knows how to take a fall with dignity.

EXT. BADA BING PARKING LOT - NIGHT

Vincent emerges into the cool night air. The neon signs cast their familiar red glow across the parking lot for what will be the last time. He walks to his car alone, the sound of his footsteps echoing across the asphalt.

The door closes behind him with a final, heavy thud.

FADE OUT.
