INT. THE RV - MORNING

The desert sun beats down on the old RV. Inside, JESSE PINKMAN watches as WALTER WHITE meticulously sets up the chemistry equipment. Steam rises from various beakers and tubes.

WALTER
(adjusting his respirator)
Pay attention, Jesse. Quality is everything. No more of your chili powder nonsense.

JESSE
Yo, Mr. White, I got it. Crystal clear. Pure chemistry.

Walter measures chemicals with precision, while Jesse observes the process carefully.

WALTER
(stern but instructive)
Hand me that phosphorus. And for God's sake, be careful with it.

Jesse carefully passes the container to Walter, showing improved attention to detail.

WALTER
(nodding approvingly)
Good. Now watch the temperature gauge. It needs to stay exactly at 185.

The cooking process proceeds smoothly, with Jesse demonstrating greater competence than before.
