INT. CROSSROADS MOTEL ROOM - VERY LATE NIGHT

Jesse sits on the edge of the bed, phone in hand. The room is dark except for the blue glow of the phone screen.

JESSE
(typing text)
"9:30 dry cleaners, then Los Pollos at 2. Need anything else from me?"

He waits, watching the three dots appear as Walter types back. A response comes quickly:

CLOSE ON PHONE SCREEN:
"Correct. Dress shirt and tie. No colors too bright. Be ready for my call at 9. Delete these messages."

JESSE
(typing)
"Got it. Deleted after reading."

Another message from Walter appears:
"Good work today. Remember - we're not asking for a job. We're offering an opportunity."

JESSE
(quietly to himself, deleting messages)
Offering an opportunity. Right.

He sets the phone down, then picks it up again to double-check his alarms one final time before turning to the window, watching a car pass slowly through the parking lot.
